# Shared zsh settings, symlinked to ~/.zshrc.shared and sourced from the tail of
# ~/.zshrc. Sourced last on purpose: it has to run after the tool inits (brew,
# rbenv, mise) have finished adding to path and fpath.
#
# Everything here is guarded or inert on a machine that doesn't need it, so the
# same file is safe to install anywhere.

# Homebrew's `brew shellenv` marks FPATH exported. Left exported it is inherited
# by the tmux server and by every child shell, which then prepend their own
# completion directories on top of the inherited copy. fpath grows on each nesting
# level, stops matching the fingerprint oh-my-zsh recorded in .zcompdump, and the
# completion cache is rebuilt from ~1300 files on every shell start.
#
# -U makes both arrays unique (it dedupes retroactively, so running here is fine);
# +x drops the export flag so children start from a clean fpath.
typeset -U path fpath
typeset +x FPATH
